reply:
Fink I spotted yer bug, mate. `fetchAll` was burnin' the candle both ends: it fires off all the async calls wiv `forEach`, then leggs it straight outta there and returns an empty array, all before any of 'em promises come back. Network log's full of requests, but the results never make it into the results pile.

Changed it to use `Promise.all` wiv `map` instead—now it actually waits for every call to come 'ome before it bolts. Keep the order bang to rights, same as the ids you chucked in.

Fixed the code:
```javascript
export async function fetchAll(ids, fetchOne) {
  return Promise.all(ids.map((id) => fetchOne(id)));
}
```

Ran the tests—all three pass. Hammered it wiv a quick smoke test too—three ids in, three records back, proper order. Widget's gonna get yer users now.

